// Tier 3 — tool-activity signals, recorded before the port derives them.
//
// These exist because the signal vocabulary cannot be re-derived: the severity
// bands, the streak lengths and the tool semantics were measured against
// benchmarks, and a port that copies the structure can still route worse. So the
// oracle's answer is recorded first and the port is written against it.
//
// Every case is one request carrying the conversation so far, because that is
// what the signals read. They stay at tier 3 until the port derives signals;
// until then it refuses tool traffic outright rather than falling open on it.
//
// What this pins, once a case resolves: the scorer's exact arithmetic (the
// recorded confidence is tanh(5*raw) and matches the source), the threshold's
// effect (0.3 escalates on one signal where 0.5 needs two), the three override
// reasons, and that the picker does not change a decision the signals made.
//
// Known gap: no case resolves on the *exploring* axis. Reading is meant to count
// as investigation, but a deep turn full of Read calls still fell open, so either
// reads are counted from somewhere other than the tool name or the axis needs a
// shape this corpus has not found. Reading the extraction settles it; until then
// the axis is unpinned, which is said here rather than papered over.
